---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="about" description={`About ${SITE.author} and ${SITE.title}.`}>
  <article class="about-body">
    <p class="post-apparatus">
      <span>colophon and the bucket glossary</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="post-title">about</h1>
    <p class="post-dek">
      A public lab notebook by <a href={SITE.portfolio}>{SITE.author}</a>, a
      developer and educator based in Antwerp. Hands-on, demo-driven write-ups
      on data science, AI, IoT, web platforms, and the occasional cultural
      side-project.
    </p>

    <h2 id="format">Format</h2>
    <p>
      Posts use one of four formats: <em>build-along</em>, <em>post-mortem</em>,
      <em>paper summary</em>, or <em>weeknote</em>. Each project post follows
      an explicit method section. Question, data, procedure, metric, result,
      limits. Set apart from the body by hairline rules and mono labels.
    </p>

    <h2 id="buckets">Buckets</h2>
    <p>
      The single-letter code in the listing tags each post by category. There
      is no hierarchy among the buckets; the letters are an index, not a rank.
    </p>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>A</strong></td>
          <td>
            <em>niche</em>. Mobility, inland shipping, e-bike, edge IoT,
            circular, cultural-public data
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>B</strong></td>
          <td>
            <em>reuse</em>. Existing artefacts (Switch-to-EU, Commensradio,
            Gaming API, etc.) treated as research field
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>C</strong></td>
          <td><em>classical ML</em> on messy real-world data</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>D</strong></td>
          <td>
            <em>methodology and statistics</em>. A/B tests, hypothesis tests,
            effect sizes, intervals
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>E</strong></td>
          <td>
            <em>writing and reading</em>. Paper summaries, proposal drafts,
            re-framings of older work
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>F</strong></td>
          <td><em>cultural</em>. Absurd, installation, off-beat</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>·</td>
          <td><em>meta</em>. About this site, stack notes, weeknotes</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="colophon">Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> on Cloudflare Pages.
      Source on <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>. Code MIT, prose CC-BY-SA.
      Cookieless analytics via Cloudflare Web Analytics. Interactive Python
      demos run client-side in <a href="https://pyodide.org">Pyodide</a>;
      nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>
    <p>
      Type set in <em>Source Serif 4</em> (body, Adobe, OFL),
      <em>Switzer</em> (display and UI, Indian Type Foundry, Fontshare), and
      <em>JetBrains Mono</em> (apparatus and code). Three families, three jobs.
      Color in OKLCH throughout. No box-shadows, by doctrine.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/rss.xml">Subscribe by RSS</a>. Or check back when you remember
      to. The cadence is biweekly when it is on, monthly when it is not.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
